 is the next continuity check with the same no-speedup discipline plus a p-bit boundary-exchange design note; it does not pretend the GateMate physical/JTAG block is resolved.\"\n    retire_if_same_verdict: true\n  - experiment_id: exp1929-p-bit-ising-v3\n    verdict: OK (conductor)\n    addressed_by: \"This task does not re-run p-bit accounting; it writes a boundary-exchange timing-ratio plan informed by new p-bit/Ising literature and current board reachability.\"\n    retire_if_same_verdict: true\n  agent_type: claude\n  model: opus\n  max_turns: 100\n  estimated_wall_time_min: 90\n  prompt: |\n    CONTEXT:\n    Repo at {project_root}, run on or after {date}. Hardware remains a correctness/reachability track.\n    .477 confirmed KV260 and PolarFire reachability, and narrowed GateMate to a physical/JTAG block with\n    raw IDCODE 0xffffffff. V478 references one-million p-bit probabilistic computers, FPGA Ising\n    decomposition, and Extropic TSU/XTR-0 writing. Do not claim speedup.\n\n    EXISTING CODE TO READ FIRST:\n    - research-hardware-wishlist.md.\n    - results/experiment_5217_hardware_continuity_v477.json.\n    - hardware docs/scripts for KV260, PolarFire, GateMate, and p-bit samplers.\n    - research-references.md V478 hardware entries.\n    - CLAUDE.md hardware/GateMate/KV260 rules.\n\n    TASK:\n    Run bounded hardware continuity checks and write a p-bit boundary-exchange timing-ratio plan for future\n    sampler work. Do not modify scripts/research_conductor.py, do not use host /dev/mmcblk preconditions for\n    KV260, and do not claim a benchmark speedup.\n\n    CONCRETE STEPS:\n    1. KV260: use SSH-only reachability, e.g. ssh -o ConnectTimeout=5 -o BatchMode=yes kria 'true'. Do not\n       inspect host /dev/mmcblk as a KV260 prerequisite.\n    2. PolarFire: run the existing reachability/hash smoke if available.\n    3. GateMate: only recheck IDCODE if the operator has changed cable/port/board setup; otherwise preserve\n       the physical/JTAG block and write the next physical action needed.\n    4. Write a short p-bit boundary-exchange timing-ratio plan that names the future workload, partitions,\n       hash/correctness checks, and what measurement would be needed before any speedup claim.\n    5. Update research-hardware-wishlist.md, ops/status.md, ops/changelog.md, and _bmad/traceability.md only\n       with factual changes.\n\n    REQUIRED ARTIFACT FIELDS:\n      kv260_reachable:\n        value: bool\n      kv260_check_method:\n        value: \"ssh_only\"\n      polarfire_reachable:\n        value: bool\n      gatemate_status:\n        value: \"reachable|blocked_physical_jtag|not_checked\"\n      gatemate_idcode_raw:\n        value: \"string or null\"\n      pbit_boundary_plan_path:\n        value: \"path\"\n      speedup_claimed:\n        value: false\n        principle: \"No .478 hardware task may claim speedup without a real end-to-end workload.\"\n      hardware_docs_updated:\n        value: bool\n      inference_substrate:\n        value: hardware_reachability_and_sampler_boundary_plan\n      honest_verdict:\n        principle: \"Must start with complete:/complete_/success:/success_ and state reachability plus no-speedup status.\"\n\n    Run command, 'Do NOT push. Do NOT modify scripts/research_conductor.py.'\n\n- id: exp5232-capstone-v478\n  milestone: 2026.07.478\n  title: \"PHASE 4 capstone -- reconcile .478 evidence, exclusions, specs, memory, and ops docs\"\n  priority: critical\n  track: planning\n  deliverable: results/experiment_5232_capstone_v478.json\n  operator_override: \"2026-05-29 operator directive: recurring milestone capstone tasks are expected and authorized when they summarize a new milestone's artifacts.\"\n  prior_failures:\n  - experiment_id: exp5219-capstone-v477\n    verdict: \"complete: v477 closed with GAP-1 building after blocked registry promotion, GAP-4 blocked by flagged/protocol validation, MMLU hidden-state path retired, self-learning memory created, zero ARC levels banked, hardware reachability maintained with no speedup claim, and flagged artifacts excluded.\"\n    addressed_by: \"This is the .478 capstone over a new artifact set; it must report registry/provenance/memory/ARC/hardware outcomes and exclude any flagged or gated artifacts.\"\n    retire_if_same_verdict: true\n  agent_type: codex\n  model: gpt-5.5\n  max_turns: 50\n  estimated_wall_time_min: 45\n  prompt: |\n    CONTEXT:\n    Repo at {project_root}, run on or after {date}. This is the .478 capstone. Do not make the milestone\n    sound better than the artifacts support. Flagged, blocked, or gated-out artifacts cannot become headline\n    claims.\n\n    EXISTING CODE TO READ FIRST:\n    - research-roadmap.yaml (the activated .478 plan).\n    - openspec/change-proposals/research-roadmap-vNEXT.md.\n    - ops/conductor-log.md entries for exp5220 through exp5231.\n    - results/experiment_5220_archive_477_activate_478.json through results/experiment_5231_hardware_continuity_pbit_boundary_v478.json.\n    - research-references.md V478 section.\n    - ops/status.md, ops/changelog.md, ops/verifier_gaps.md, ops/arc_solve_registry.yaml, ops/exclusion_manifest.yaml.\n    - _bmad/traceability.md and relevant openspec/capabilities/*/spec.md files.\n\n    TASK:\n    Reconcile the milestone: summarize what changed, what remains blocked, what must be retired or excluded,\n    and whether the continuous self-learning mandate was met.\n\n    CONCRETE STEPS:\n    1. Read every .478 result artifact directly. Do not infer success from task title.\n    2. Identify headline-eligible claims only when artifacts passed gates and adversarial checks.\n    3. Record GAP-1 status, GAP-4 status, VerIbmc solver-feedback status, typed-memory status, ARC status,\n       KAN certificate status, and hardware status.\n    4. Update openspec, _bmad/traceability.md, ops/status.md, ops/changelog.md, ops/verifier_gaps.md, and\n       research-references.md as needed.\n    5. Run relevant lint/spec-coverage/unit checks and record pass/fail honestly.\n    6. Confirm scripts/research_conductor.py was not modified.\n\n    REQUIRED ARTIFACT FIELDS:\n      gap1_final_status:\n        value: \"promoted|blocked|unchanged\"\n      gap4_final_status:\n        value: \"clean_positive|clean_null|blocked|unchanged\"\n      solver_feedback_status:\n        value: \"positive|null|blocked|not_run\"\n      continuous_self_learning_satisfied:\n        value: bool\n      arc_new_levels_banked:\n        value: \"list\"\n      arc_reproducible_total_levels_delta:\n        value: int\n      kan_certificate_status:\n        value: \"produced|blocked|not_run\"\n      hardware_status:\n        value: \"one-line summary\"\n      flagged_artifacts_excluded:\n        value: bool\n      docs_reconciled:\n        value: bool\n      validation_commands_run:\n        value: \"list of commands and pass/fail\"\n      research_conductor_py_untouched_confirmed:\n        value: bool\n      inference_substrate:\n        value: aggregation_from_milestone_artifacts\n      honest_verdict:\n        principle: \"Must start with complete:/complete_/success:/success_ and state the true .478 outcome without laundering flagged or gated artifacts.\"\n\n    Run command, 'Do NOT push. Do NOT modify scripts/research_conductor.py.'\n",
